## Hard Rules (Always Enforced — No Exceptions)

1. **NEVER activate `pipeline_v2.py`** — `ci/check_pipeline_v2_guard.py` hard-rejects any touch
2. **Read the current file before editing** — never write from memory
3. **`make push` before any remote push** — runs `make pr-check` + `git push`; API push only if git fails AND pr-check already passed this session
4. **`make update m=X`** for all module upgrades — never bare `odoo-bin` outside Docker
5. **Staging → Production** — never merge features directly to Production
6. **`sudo()` needs inline justification** — comment on the same line why
7. **New models need ACL** — `ir.model.access.csv` in the same module
8. **No credentials in code** — use `.env.local` or Odoo system params
9. **Additive migrations only** — no column/table drops without explicit approval
10. **`ruff check && ruff format` before every push** — no exceptions, even for "trivial" changes

